  "notes": "Farmland Partners Inc. (NYSE: FPI). Internally-managed REIT focused on row-crop farmland (corn, soybeans, wheat, cotton, rice) across 16 US states. Data sourced from SEC EDGAR (CIK 0001591670) 10-K and 10-Q filings plus IR releases. 2023-2024 saw a major capital-recycling program: ~$200M+ of property sales including the December 2024 $289M Murray Wise-brokered portfolio sale that returned $1.15/sh special dividend in early 2025. Acreage declined from ~150k+ at peak to ~71.6k by 2025 reflecting both dispositions and management agreements transferred. Net debt computed from total mortgage notes + bonds + lines of credit less cash. NOI from supplemental investor packages (REIT-style: rental revenue less property opex). EBITDA computed as operating income + D&A unless company disclosed Adjusted EBITDA. propertyBookMM = net real estate at depreciated cost (US GAAP). Historical FY2014-FY2018 backfill from 10-K Selected Financial Data tables (audited); FY14 partial year reflects April 2014 IPO; FY17 reflects American Farmland Co. (AFCO) merger closing Feb 2017.",
